        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "742ebfb3-885b-5430-b676-237b13da31a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gareth Evans, Michael Winner, Mike Leeder\n- Works: The Raid, The Raid 2, Fearless, The Man with the Iron Fists, Man of Tai Chi, Ultimate Justice, Rogue One\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, film editor, action choreographer, producer, restaurant critic\n- Topics: Asian cinema, international cult and action cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Winner was born on 30 October 1935 and died on 21 January 2013.\n- Gareth Huw Evans was born in 1980.\n- Fearless was released in 2006, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- The Raid was released in 2011.\n- The Man with the Iron Fists was released in 2012, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- Man of Tai Chi was released in 2013, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- Gareth Huw Evans is a Welsh film director, screenwriter, film editor, and action choreographer.\n- Michael Winner was an English film director and producer, and he was also a restaurant critic for The Sunday Times.\n- The Raid 2 is a sequel to Gareth Evans's 2011 film The Raid.\n- The Raid 2 was released in 2014, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- Ultimate Justice was released in 2016, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- Rogue One was released in 2016, and Mike Leeder worked on it.\n- Mike Leeder is considered an authority on Asian cinema and international cult and action cinema.\n- Mike Leeder is known for work both in front of and behind the camera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
